# {{ project_name }}

{{ description }}

An MCP server built with [FastMCP](https://github.com/jlowin/fastmcp), generated from
[mcpserver-template](https://github.com/zerotropism/mcpserver-template): `{{ backend }}` backend,
`{{ transport }}` transport{% if transport == "http" %}, `{{ auth }}` authentication{% endif %}.
The server only knows the `TaskRepository` protocol; the backend is injected.

## Run

```bash
uv sync --all-groups
uv run pytest
{%- if transport == "stdio" %}
uv run {{ project_slug }}          # serves over stdio
{%- else %}
uv run {{ project_slug }}          # serves streamable HTTP on http://127.0.0.1:8000/mcp
{%- endif %}
```
{%- if transport == "http" %}

| Variable | Default | Role |
|---|---|---|
| `MCP_HOST` | `127.0.0.1` | interface to listen on (`0.0.0.0` in the Docker image) |
| `MCP_PORT` | `8000` | port to listen on |
{%- if auth == "bearer" %}
| `MCP_JWT_PUBLIC_KEY` | none | PEM public key that signs the tokens |
| `MCP_JWT_JWKS_URI` | none | or a JWKS URL, for keys published by an identity provider |
| `MCP_JWT_ISSUER` | none | expected `iss` claim, recommended |
| `MCP_JWT_AUDIENCE` | none | expected `aud` claim, recommended |
{%- endif %}
{%- if backend == "sqlite" %}
| `DB_PATH` | per-user data directory | SQLite file |
{%- endif %}
{%- if auth == "bearer" %}

Every request needs `Authorization: Bearer <JWT>`. The server refuses to start without
`MCP_JWT_PUBLIC_KEY` or `MCP_JWT_JWKS_URI`, and answers 401 to a request without a valid token.
{%- endif %}
{%- endif %}

## Try it from a client

[mcp-servers-cli](https://pypi.org/project/mcp-servers-cli/) lists what the server exposes and
lets a model drive its tools:

```bash
{%- if transport == "stdio" %}
uvx mcp-servers-cli inspect --stdio "uv run --directory $PWD {{ project_slug }}"
uvx mcp-servers-cli agent "Add a task: write the report, then list pending tasks" \
  --model qwen3.5:4b-mlx --stdio "uv run --directory $PWD {{ project_slug }}"
{%- else %}
{%- if auth == "bearer" %}
export MCP_TOKEN=<a JWT accepted by the server>
{%- endif %}
uvx mcp-servers-cli inspect --http http://127.0.0.1:8000/mcp
uvx mcp-servers-cli agent "Add a task: write the report, then list pending tasks" \
  --model qwen3.5:4b-mlx --http http://127.0.0.1:8000/mcp
{%- endif %}
```

`filter_tasks` takes a nested object: small local models struggle with it. See the measured
requirements in the mcp-servers-cli README before picking a model.
{%- if backend == "sqlite" %}

## Storage

Tasks are stored in SQLite, at `DB_PATH` when it is set, otherwise in the per-user data
directory (`platformdirs`), never in the current directory.
{%- if transport == "stdio" %} MCP clients forward only a short
list of environment variables to a stdio server, so pass `DB_PATH` explicitly:

```bash
uvx mcp-servers-cli inspect --env DB_PATH=$PWD/tasks.db --stdio "uv run --directory $PWD {{ project_slug }}"
```
{%- endif %}
{%- endif %}
{%- if transport == "http" %}

## Docker

The image is built from the lock file, runs as an unprivileged user and listens on port 8000:

```bash
uv lock
docker build -t {{ project_slug }} .
docker run --rm -p 8000:8000{% if backend == "sqlite" %} -v {{ project_slug }}-data:/data{% endif %}{% if auth == "bearer" %} -e MCP_JWT_PUBLIC_KEY="$(cat public.pem)"{% endif %} {{ project_slug }}
```
{%- if backend == "sqlite" %}

The database lives in the `/data` volume.
{%- endif %}
{%- endif %}

## MCP API

| Kind | Name |
|---|---|
| Tools | `add_task`, `complete_task`, `complete_tasks`, `delete_task`, `filter_tasks` |
| Resources | `tasks://all`, `tasks://pending`, `tasks://completed`, `tasks://stats`, `tasks://today`, `tasks://weekly-summary` |
| Prompts | `task_summary_prompt`, `priority_analysis_prompt`, `scheduling_prompt`, `weekly_review_prompt` |

`filter_tasks` takes one `TaskFilter`; every criterion is optional and they combine with AND:
`{"task_filter": {"status": "pending", "keyword": "report"}}`. Errors are raised as MCP errors;
no tool returns an `{"error": ...}` dictionary.

## Layout

```
src/{{ module_name }}/
├── models.py              Task, TaskFilter, TaskStats
├── repository.py          TaskRepository protocol and TaskNotFoundError
├── repositories/
│   └── {{ backend }}.py          the {{ backend }} backend
└── server.py              tools, resources and prompts; repository injected
tests/                     same contract suite for any backend
```

Adding a backend means one class implementing the protocol's seven methods; the tests in
`tests/test_repositories.py` apply to it unchanged once the `repo` fixture builds it.

## Keeping up with the template

The answers given at generation are in `.copier-answers.yml`. To bring in a newer version of
the template:

```bash
uvx copier update
```

Commit `uv.lock` after the first `uv sync`: Dependabot{% if transport == "http" %} and the Docker build{% endif %} need it.
